From 8c03a3e0626c0e4a3f3533a488667a0fb03cc22c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:56:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native V2 index bounds follow the consensus
 block-size limit

Same fix as the Rust index: the native V2 index skipped valid large
blocks ("staging capacity") because of the fixed 4096-transaction,
65536-change and 32 MiB staging bounds.

lotus_v2::Bounds (model.h) derives the transaction, change and staging
bounds from the consensus block-size limit, with the same constants and
shortest-encoding argument as Rust. V2Db, ReadSnapshot and V2Service take
it; connect, the undo validation of disconnect, receipt/undo/batch checks
and explorer reads use it. The ABC host passes the configured maximum
block size, at least the 1 GB adaptive ceiling, within 32 bits, and
derives the transaction and change limits from it. Stored records are
unchanged, so DB dumps stay equal to Rust's.

Tests mirror Rust: staging_covers_shortest_encodings,
block_over_former_fixed_bounds_is_indexed (4100 transactions, over 32 MiB
reserved, connected and disconnected), small explicit bounds in the
capacity and transaction-bound tests, and the service block_bytes
boundary.

Tier: V2
